Description: antinomie: debug engine: hardware breakpoints and watchpoints
Author: MikiMiku <jonathanirvinjo@gmail.com>
Origin: project
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-20

Instruction breakpoints and write or access watchpoints in the debug registers, through the kernel's own breakpoint facility (register_user_hw_breakpoint), for every thread of the group. Nothing is written into the program's memory, which is the answer to direct reads of its own code, and nothing is placed in the virtual debug-register state that a tracer or a SIGTRAP would reveal: a tracer of the sample reads zeros, and no signal is raised.  The four slots are one pool shared by all hardware kinds; BP_SET with none left is -ENOSPC, a misaligned or odd length -EINVAL. A hit stops the group like any other event (HWBREAK, WATCH with the breakpoint's address and the kind that fired). A thread resumes past an instruction breakpoint it stopped at without the breakpoint firing again (RF), a watchpoint that fires with the engine's single step is reported in preference to the step, and threads c

